# Rebound Physiotherapy — Project Guide

## Project Overview

A static, single-page business website for **Rebound Physiotherapy and Rehabilitation Center**, a physiotherapy clinic based in Payyanur, Kannur, Kerala, India.

- **Live site**: https://www.reboundphysiotherapy.in
- **Repo**: https://github.com/nithincspnr/reboundphysio
- **Purpose**: Business presence site — showcase services, team, testimonials, and contact information for the clinic.
- **No build step required** for deployment — the site is pure HTML/CSS/JS that can be served from any static host.

---

## Tech Stack

| Layer   | Technology                                                                                      |
| ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Markup  | HTML5                                                                                           |
| Styling | Bootstrap 5 (via SCSS customization) + custom CSS                                               |
| Scripts | jQuery 3.4, vanilla JavaScript, WOW.js, OwlCarousel 2.3, CounterUp                              |
| SCSS    | Custom `scss/bootstrap.scss` overrides Bootstrap variables, compiled to `css/bootstrap.min.css` |
| Hosting | GitHub Pages (CNAME file for custom domain)                                                     |

### Third-party libraries (loaded via CDN)

- **jQuery 3.4** — `code.jquery.com`
- **Bootstrap 5** — `cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.0.0`
- **Font Awesome 5** — icons
- **Bootstrap Icons 1.4** — icons

### Third-party libraries (vendored in `lib/`)

- **WOW.js** — scroll animations (fadeIn for sections, fadeInUp for cards)
- **OwlCarousel 2.3** — carousels (header, testimonials)
- **Easing** — jQuery easing animations
- **Waypoints** — scroll-triggered events
- **CounterUp** — animated number counters
- **Animate.css** — base animation library (WOW.js dependency)

---

## Project Structure

```
reboundphysio/
├── index.html              # Single-page site (all sections in one file)
├── CNAME                   # Custom domain for GitHub Pages
├── README.md
├── css/
│   ├── bootstrap.min.css   # Compiled Bootstrap (from SCSS)
│   └── style.css           # Custom CSS (~450 lines)
├── scss/
│   └── bootstrap.scss      # Bootstrap variable overrides → compiled to css/bootstrap.min.css
├── js/
│   └── main.js             # jQuery-based site functionality
├── lib/                    # Vendored third-party JS/CSS libs
│   ├── wow/
│   ├── easing/
│   ├── waypoints/
│   ├── counterup/
│   ├── owlcarousel/
│   └── animate/
└── img/                    # Team photos, service images, logo, favicon
```

---

## Design System

### Colors

```css
--primary: #00adef; /* Sky blue — main accent */
--primary-dark: #0095cc;
--primary-light: #e6f7fe;
--light: #eff5ff; /* Light blue-tinted background */
--dark: #1b2c51; /* Deep navy — headings, hero background */
--body: #5a6072; /* Body text */
--border: #dce7f5; /* Subtle borders */
--surface: #ffffff; /* Card/surface backgrounds */
```

Used across: buttons, links, icons, borders, hover states, card accents, hero background.

### Typography

- **Body**: `'Open Sans', sans-serif` (400, 500, 600 weights)
- **Headings**: `'Roboto', sans-serif` (500, 700, 900 weights)
- Heading color: `var(--dark)`
- Body color: `var(--body)` — `#5a6072`

### Border & Radius

- `--radius: 12px` (cards, buttons, containers)
- `--radius-sm: 8px` (small elements, buttons)
- `--radius-lg: 20px` (hero visual, large images)
- `--border: #dce7f5` (subtle borders on cards)

### Shadows

- `--shadow-sm` — 0 2px 8px rgba(27, 44, 81, 0.06)
- `--shadow-md` — 0 8px 30px rgba(27, 44, 81, 0.08)
- `--shadow-lg` — 0 20px 60px rgba(27, 44, 81, 0.10)

### Spacing

- Bootstrap's standard spacing scale.
- Sections use `py-5` (3rem padding top/bottom).
- Cards use `g-4` gutters.

---

## HTML Conventions

- **Single-page layout** — sections are anchored by IDs (`#about-us`, `#services`, `#team`, `#testimonials`)
- **Section pattern**: `container-xxl py-5 > container > row > col`
- **Section header pattern**: centered `text-center mx-auto mb-5 wow fadeInUp` with a `.section-badge` span and an `.section-title` h2
- **All scroll animations** use WOW.js with `wow fadeIn` or `wow fadeInUp` classes plus `data-wow-delay="0.1s"` (incremented per item)
  - `fadeIn` = simple opacity transition (used for larger blocks like topbar, navbar, hero halves, about columns, footer)
  - `fadeInUp` = scale + opacity entrance (used for card grids: services, team, testimonials, section headers)
- **Images** use `img-fluid` for responsiveness
- **External links** open with `target="_blank"` (WhatsApp, social media)

### Page Sections (in order)

1. **Spinner** — loading overlay (`#spinner`)
2. **Topbar** — address, hours, phone, social icons (hidden on mobile)
3. **Navbar** — sticky top navigation with glassmorphism effect, scroll-linked `.scrolled` class
4. **Header/Hero** — dark gradient hero with carousel and stats counters
5. **About** — image stack (main + inset) + description with feature list
6. **Services** — 4 service cards in a 2×2 grid with hover accent bar
7. **Team** — profile cards in a responsive grid with hover zoom
8. **Testimonials** — centered carousel with quote cards
9. **Footer** — address, services links, quick links with accent top border
10. **Back-to-top** — floating button

### Section Badge Pattern

```html
<span class="section-badge mb-3">Section Label</span>
<h2 class="section-title">Section Heading</h2>
<p class="section-subtitle">Optional description text.</p>
```

The `.section-badge` is a pill with a dot indicator before the text, replacing the old `border rounded-pill py-1 px-4` pattern.

---

## CSS Conventions

### File: `css/style.css`

- Custom properties in `:root` for all design tokens
- Component-prefixed classes: `.service-card`, `.team-card`, `.testimonial-card`, `.section-badge`, `.section-title`
- Cards use `::before` pseudo-elements for accent hover effects (e.g., top bar on service cards)
- Hero uses a full dark gradient background (`#1b2c51` → darker) with subtle SVG pattern overlay
- Navbar uses `backdrop-filter: blur(10px)` for glassmorphism effect
- Hover transitions use `0.4s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1)` — a smooth ease-out curve
- WOW.js animations are customized: `fadeIn` = simple opacity, `fadeInUp` = scale(0.96) + opacity (no translateY)
- Responsive overrides at 992px (tablet), 768px (mobile)
- OwlCarousel overrides for header dots/nav and testimonial nav buttons

### SCSS (Bootstrap overrides)

- File: `scss/bootstrap.scss`
- Customizes: `$primary`, `$light`, `$dark`, font families, border radius values, border colors, body text color
- Compiled to `css/bootstrap.min.css` via: `cd scss && sass bootstrap.scss ../css/bootstrap.min.css --style compressed`

---

## JavaScript Conventions

### File: `js/main.js`

- All code wrapped in jQuery `(function ($) { ... })(jQuery);`
- Uses `"use strict";`
- **Spinner**: auto-hides on page load (1ms delay)
- **WOW.js**: initialized on load
- **Sticky navbar**: adds `shadow-sm` and `.scrolled` class when scrolled past 300px; hides above viewport initially
- **Back-to-top**: fades in/out past 300px scroll, smooth scroll up with easeInOutExpo
- **CounterUp**: animated stats on `.header` counters
- **Carousels**: OwlCarousel configs — header carousel (autoplay off, fadeOutLeft, dots, nav arrows), testimonials (center mode, responsive: 1 item mobile, 2 items tablet)

---

## How to Make Changes

### Adding a new section to the page

1. Follow the existing section pattern: `container-xxl py-5 > container > row > col`
2. Use the standard header pattern: `section-badge` + `section-title` + optional `section-subtitle`
3. Add WOW.js animation classes with staggered delays (increment by 0.1s per item)
4. Add a corresponding nav link in `.navbar-nav`

### Adding a team member

1. Add the image to `img/` (square crop recommended)
2. Copy an existing `col.wow.fadeInUp` block in `#team`
3. Update `src`, `alt`, `h5` name, `p.team-role` title, and optional `small` qualifications

### Adding a service

1. Copy an existing `.service-card` block in `#services`
2. Choose an appropriate Font Awesome icon class for `.icon-wrap i`
3. Update title and description text
4. Increment `data-wow-delay` by 0.1s from the previous sibling

### Adding a testimonial

1. Add image to `img/` (square crop, 72×72px or larger)
2. Copy a `.testimonial-card` block in `#testimonials`
3. Update `src`, `alt`, `blockquote` text, author name, and role

### Styling changes

- For Bootstrap-level changes (colors, fonts, radius): edit `scss/bootstrap.scss` and recompile
- For custom component styles: edit `css/style.css`
- Recompile SCSS: `cd scss && sass bootstrap.scss ../css/bootstrap.min.css --style compressed`

### Deployment

- Push to `main` branch — GitHub Pages auto-deploys
- `CNAME` file keeps the custom domain intact
- No build step needed

---

## Important Conventions to Preserve

- **Keep the single-page architecture** — don't split into multiple HTML files unless there's a strong need
- **Maintain the color scheme** — primary blue (`#00adef`), light (`#eff5ff`), dark navy (`#1b2c51`)
- **Follow the animation pattern** — WOW.js with staggered delays, smooth cubic-bezier transitions
- **Use semantic IDs** for anchor navigation (e.g., `#services`, `#team`)
- **Keep jQuery-based JS** in `main.js` following the existing module pattern
- **Images should be optimized** for web before adding
- **External links** (WhatsApp, social) open in new tabs
- **All phone numbers and addresses** should match the business details exactly
- **Card patterns** — service cards use `.service-card` with top accent bar hover, team cards use `.team-card` with image zoom hover, testimonials use `.testimonial-card` with open-quote pseudo-element
